<title>BELGIUM: EU farmers to pay for exceeding milk quotas.</title>
<headline>EU farmers to pay for exceeding milk quotas.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union dairy farmers are facing substantial super levy payments according to the latest milk production estimates, a Commission offical said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Milk production in the EU is 1.1 million tonnes over the quota and farmers will have to pay the super levy in those countries which are over.</p>
<p>&quot;The state is not allowed to pay. The charge falls on individual farmers,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The provisional estimates from member states forecast national production over the limit by:-</p>
<p>		     Excess tonnes   Italy	     470,000 tonnes</p>
<p> France	    158,000 tonnes  Britain	   145,000 tonnes</p>
<p> Spain	     126,000 tonnes  Netherlands	90,000 tonnes</p>
<p> Ireland	    48,000 tonnes  Denmark	    23,000 tonnes</p>
<p> Belgium	    18,000 tonnes  Germany	    16,000 tonnes</p>
<p> Luxembourg	  3,000 tonnes</p>
<p>Production in Portugal is put at 200,000 tonnes under quota.</p>
</text>
